We can build on the code above by using `with_columns` in place of `select` and introducing a `when-then-otherwise` expression to clamp values outside the 5th to 95th percentile range:

::: {#2c3f58cf .cell execution_count=42}
``` {.python .cell-code}
(liquor_sales
 .with_columns(Percentile_95=pl.col('Volume_Gal').quantile(0.95, interpolation='linear'),
               Percentile_05=pl.col('Volume_Gal').quantile(0.05, interpolation='linear'))
 .with_columns(pl.when(pl.col('Volume_Gal') > pl.col('Percentile_95'))
               .then(pl.col('Percentile_95'))
               .when(pl.col('Volume_Gal') < pl.col('Percentile_05'))
               .then(pl.col('Percentile_05'))
               .otherwise(pl.col('Volume_Gal'))
               .alias('Volume_Winsorized'))
 .select('Date','City','Volume_Gal','Volume_Winsorized')
)
```

